WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
I've spent the last 6 years learning how

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.560
social media works and the results are

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.360
in. I've got 25 million followers, 500

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.880
million views a month. I figured out. I

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.800
know how it all works and I'm going to

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.800
teach you it today.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.280
So, number one on my list of things that

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.800
you need to know, be authentic. You have

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.560
to tell your story, you have to share

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.600
your reason why you're doing it. You

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.040
probably all know my story. I was 15

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.960
years old when my father died and I was

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.759
kicked out of home. I was homeless and I

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.520
tried to get a job and I couldn't get

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.880
one. I tried to go to social services

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:39.760
and get help and they said no. I was on

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.000
my own. And the only thing that I could

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.200
do was start a business. I didn't want

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.320
to be an entrepreneur, I needed to be an

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.720
entrepreneur. And telling you that story

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.200
helps you understand why I'm doing

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:53.200
something and you need to tell the same

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:56.280
story. Don't try and be someone else.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.760
You're unique and you must play to that

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.000
strength. By the way, I've written a

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.440
book called What's Your Story? If you're

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.360
not sure how to craft a story or make

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.800
your story real, the link's down below.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.000
This book can help you do it, but being

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.480
authentic is key. So, learn to know who

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.080
you are. If, for example, you are

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.480
building a business and you perhaps are

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.040
tempted to start giving advice to

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.600
people, perhaps you're not there yet.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.160
Better instead talk about what you're

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.320
struggling with and what you're learning

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.000
along the way and building public that

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.440
way as opposed to pretend to be a guru,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.680
right? I see a lot of people pretending

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.160
to be something they're not. You don't

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.000
need to do that. The second thing I want

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.640
to teach you is you've got to

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.400
tailor-make your content for each

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:32.080
channel. A lot of people when they go to

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.400
do social media, what they really want

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.680
to do is a quick video, put it up and

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.720
get millions of views. But the real way

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.280
to make social media work is to think

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.320
about the channels that you're on. And

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.920
one simple hack is each of the apps,

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:48.480
like it if you actually tailor the

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.080
videos inside the app. And when you go

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.080
and load up a video, for example, on

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.760
TikTok, use the in-app edit to make the

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:57.080
screen caption really clear cuz when

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.360
people see a video, they want to know

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.320
what the video's about. And then the

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.720
hook, of course, hopefully is

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.200
interesting. You need a hook on a video,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.280
but that will draw people in. And that's

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.360
what you need initially to get people to

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.560
watch video, but what I'm getting to is

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.399
like that platform likes to think that

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.720
the content is tailor-made for that

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:14.520
platform. So, Snapchat, YouTube, TikTok,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.480
Instagram, go in and edit your video in

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.040
those apps. It's a hack that not a lot

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.240
of people have shared because I think

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.040
people are lazy and they don't want to

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.320
hear it. Don't be lazy. That's a very

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.720
important part of being sure social

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.600
media works. Do [snorts] the work. I'm

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.920
also, while I'm at it, tailor-making

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.280
each of the platforms also means going

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.160
into the comments and replying on each

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.360
platform, ideally yourself, but equally,

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.800
if you need to go and get help to do it,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.920
but reply to people. Give them

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.480
information. You can even use tools like

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.120
ManyChat, which don't sponsor this

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.400
video, but it's a good tool, where you

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.120
can basically get the app to apply to

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.200
your comments and engage with people.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.880
Send them information. Send them

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.640
follow-up. But learn to engage in the

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.200
comments. Again, not a lot of people do

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.320
that, and they get a bit lazy and they

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.040
can't be bothered. They might check it

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.120
for the first 10 minutes and then leave

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.160
it. You're leaving engagement on the

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.160
table. If someone asked your question

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.880
and you reply with an answer and or a

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.160
question, they reply again, the

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.959
algorithm likes to see on all platforms

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.959
engagement with the audience in the

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:11.560
comments. And I will just finally say on

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:13.680
something like Snapchat, they want you

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.880
to make the actual video in the app.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.040
Recently, they launched a feature where

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.519
you can see if the video was made in the

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.880
app. So, you record the actual video in

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:23.840
the actual app, and then it shows on

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:26.400
Snapchat that it was recorded on

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.560
Snapchat. It wasn't an uploaded video,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.120
it was created in Snapchat. And the way

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.920
you can also look at other platforms is

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.800
on stories for Instagram, you want to

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.360
create the video in real time, but

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.600
actually recording the story in the

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.000
moment. Don't make a standard video and

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.720
upload it into stories. Create an

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.280
original video. And the general

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.880
principle for every platform, but I will

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.200
go into this more depth another time,

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:50.200
but the basic principle is make the app

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.240
believe that it's an original piece of

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.120
content for the platform that you're

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:57.440
uploading on. And that will ensure the

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.200
platform thinks it's unique content it

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:01.697
should push out. The third thing I want

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.960
you to understand is how important data

00:04:01.697 --> 00:04:05.800
[music] is. Now, data on social media is

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:09.480
really split into two camps. The first

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:11.880
is what does each video data show you?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:14.040
Is the hook getting retention? Are

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.239
people staying on the video and are they

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.920
watching it again? If you can see in the

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:19.799
data that they're not watching the video

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.239
to the end, you might want to re-edit

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:23.320
the video and put it out again.

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:25.800
Basically, what the platforms want is

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.919
for the video to get watched initially

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.760
and then for it to be repeated so you

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:30.960
stay on platform. And it's fine to

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.960
understand how these platforms work.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.400
They make money if people stay on

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:35.680
platform, right? So, they want you to

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.720
make content that people engage with.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:40.720
So, looking at the data to see is the

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.200
graph showing a retention? Are people

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.840
staying on the video and are they

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.000
watching it again? Will help you

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.480
understand whether you've edited it

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.640
right. The other side of the data that

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:52.680
you need to think about is every time

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:55.480
you put a video out, you ideally want

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.520
someone to join your mailing list. But

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.200
you want people to join your community.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.200
So, one of my ambitions with the 25

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.160
million followers I have is to get you

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.280
guys to sign up to my mailing list. And

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:05.880
by the way, if you want to, there is a

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.320
link down below in this YouTube video.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.000
But my point is, of course you have to

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.560
offer value to people to do that. So, in

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.080
my case, I'm doing a weekly newsletter

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.080
teaching people all the latest trends

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.560
and business news that they need to know

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.720
to make their business successful. Of

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.440
course, you need a hook, give people

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.960
reason to sign up. Every time a video

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.960
goes out, I don't want to rely on any

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.919
social media platform in the future

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.840
actually working, actually not blocking

00:05:24.919 --> 00:05:28.240
me, actually not to suddenly suppressing

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.919
my videos. So, every time I make a

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.200
video, I want to encourage people to

00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:35.440
join my mailing list in some way, even

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.840
if it's in the body text down below or I

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.200
encourage people in the video to do it

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.480
directly. But that's what I want you to

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.320
also think about because if you have a

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.520
database of a thousand people that you

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.000
can email about your business, your

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.480
service, your product or ask them to

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.520
promote your business, service or

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.000
product. That's so much more powerful

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.400
than maybe a million views on a video

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.000
where there's no engagement, right?

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.600
Where there's no interaction. So,

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.400
ultimately, collecting data and

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.840
analyzing data is a real key part for

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.880
making social media sustainable in the

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.920
future and successful in the short term.

