How are other people doing it? I do

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:39.000
street content. It's not an original

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:40.960
idea. It was an original execution. Use

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.680
the system, don't let the system use

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:45.200
you. That's how you get rich in life.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:47.760
You learn to leverage the place, you

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:49.520
learn to leverage the platforms, so your

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:52.040
life's better. Don't let them leverage

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.760
you. Get the balance right. The final

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:55.960
thing I want to teach you is probably

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:58.320
the most important and equally one of

00:09:55.960 --> 00:10:00.520
the hardest to actually achieve. Most

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:03.280
people, when they do social media, they

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:07.240
think it's one person and a camera

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:09.320
making content is a team sport. Behind

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:11.200
the camera right now, I have my two

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.480
colleagues helping me do this video. And

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:15.440
without them, this quality of this video

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:17.000
would be lower, perhaps even the way I

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.360
deliver it, even though I know business.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:20.760
I've been doing business a very long

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.480
time, I still might miss something.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.960
Because we can't do it on our own. The

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.480
school system teaches us to sit down and

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.640
do an exam on our own. And if you get an

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:28.440
A, you're successful. And if you get a

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:30.000
D, you're a failure. In the real world,

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:32.680
every business I've ever built is done

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.040
in teams. So as quickly as possible, you

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.560
want to try and build out a team. Now,

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:37.040
everybody's different, but I'll give you

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.640
a little advice on what team structure

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.440
to go for. To make social media very

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.080
sustainable, you really need a few

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:43.480
different key people. And you can be any

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.720
one of these people yourself or bring

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.839
someone in. And I'll teach you quickly

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.839
how to bring someone in so it doesn't

00:10:45.839 --> 00:10:49.760
cost you a lot of money. But first, of

00:10:47.839 --> 00:10:51.200
course, you need a good camera person,

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:53.080
someone that understands how to use a

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.400
camera and make sure they capture the

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.360
footage that you are producing. The

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.800
second thing is you need an editor. Now,

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.480
the editor and the cameraman can be the

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.120
same person. They don't necessarily have

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.320
to be. And sometimes, people that are

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.760
good at camera work doesn't mean they're

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.440
good at editing and vice versa. But of

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.280
course, holy grail would be both. All

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.640
the business knowledge is in my head,

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:11.400
but I think you need someone often to

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.800
structure out what is the content, how

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.280
will it play. Storytelling is very

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:15.760
important. But you kind of need that

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:17.680
that team. And then ideally, you need

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.839
someone who's focused on posting up the

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.720
videos. Again, these all can be one

00:11:19.839 --> 00:11:23.200
person if you get lucky. But I want you

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:24.960
to know how I've structured it. Of

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.520
course, my channel's at massive volume

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:28.360
now, so I can afford to have all of

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:30.480
those people part-time. But it wasn't

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:32.000
always the case. Now, the hack for

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.800
getting a team on board is actually a

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.320
hack for making every business

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.920
successful. Share the upside. There are

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.840
716,000

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:41.560
kids in England right now that can't

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.880
find work. They come out of uni and they

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:45.440
can't find a job. That's a lot of talent

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:46.840
that isn't earning right now. But if you

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:48.600
said to them, "Hey, let's start a

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:50.960
YouTube channel teaching people how to

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.280
play chess and I'll give you 50% of the

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.280
revenue that the YouTube video

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:55.680
produces." Perhaps that person will give

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:57.120
you their time for free. Perhaps they'll

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.440
come and join you as a co-founder in the

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.320
business. Share upside in your business

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.400
is one of the biggest hacks I personally

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:05.040
learned. I don't want 100% of a business

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:06.520
I don't enjoy doing every day. I'd

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.640
rather have 10% of something that's

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:10.320
having a big impact in the world and I'm

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:12.480
able to do it with people I love working

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:14.520
with that are working as hard and care

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:16.480
as much as I do. And that's worth giving

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:17.600
up equity to. Despite what you hear

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:20.280
about having to have it all for

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:22.800
yourself, trust me, success comes

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:24.080
working in teams. I hope you've enjoyed

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.000
today's video. I want to give a thousand

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.880
pounds away to anyone that makes a

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:30.280
social media post sharing what they've

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:31.360
learned here or just putting up a video

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.320
from what you've learned today and

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:34.160
tagging me in it. I'm going to give a

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:37.600
thousand pounds to one person. Thank you

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.600
so much for listening today. Goodbye.

